  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA front sinks southward through the area this weekend while a low \nwanders out of the Central Plains and into the Southeastern US. More \nshowers and thunderstorms are expected to traverse the area ahead of \nand along the front today, with continued potential for localized \nflash flooding to occur in heavy downpours. Poor drainage areas and \nlocations that recently received heavy rain will be the most \nsusceptible to flooding today. No changes have been made to the \nFlood Watch, which remains in effect for the bulk of the area until \nSunday morning. In addition to flooding, a few stronger storms \ncould produce gusty winds.\n\nWhile precipitation coverage should lessen behind the front \novernight, lingering moisture is expected to support some renewed \nactivity, primarily in the afternoon and evening hours, early next \nweek.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nDrier weather briefly takes hold Tuesday into Wednesday amid a \nwarming trend, then another system brings increased\nprecipitation chances for the end of next week. That being \nsaid, the details remain a bit murky as to the timing of this \npotential system.",
